# Dual input (gamepad + mouse/keyboard)

Every interactive screen and overlay in TinyTBS must be fully usable with **gamepad** and with **mouse + keyboard**. Players may switch devices mid-session.

## Rules

- Drive menu / overlay focus and confirm through **`GameCommand`** (`GameCommandService` + screen `HandleInput` / `HandleGamepadNavigation`), not Gum `UseGamepadDefaults` (it double-steps D-pad/stick and steals focus onto scrollbars).
- Mouse: Gum clicks on buttons stay valid; do not require gamepad-only paths.
- Keyboard: arrows/WASD / Enter-Space map to the same `GameCommand` values as D-pad/stick / A (see `DefaultInputBindings`).
- Greyed controls: `IsEnabled = false` **and** `Visual.HasEvents = false` so they cannot take focus.
- New screens: after `GumService.Update`, call focus navigation that uses `WasPressed(Navigate*)` / `Confirm` / `Back`/`Info` as appropriate — same pattern as Main Menu, Content Library, New Game, shop, pause.

